<title>UK: Czarnikow details world sugar output forecast.</title>
<headline>Czarnikow details world sugar output forecast.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of Czarnikow Sugar's latest estimate of world 1996/97 sugar production and 1997 consumption, issued on Thursday.</p>
<p>All figures are in thousands of tonnes, raw value.</p>
<p>BEET sugar output</p>
<p>	     estimate 1996/97	  1995/96</p>
<p> France		  4,593	    4,601</p>
<p> Germany		 4,554	    4,158</p>
<p> EU TOTAL	     17,932	   17,026</p>
<p> Russia		  1,845	    2,240</p>
<p> Ukraine		 2,935	    3,788</p>
<p> Ex-USSR TOTAL	 5,256	    6,558</p>
<p> Poland		  2,497	    1,714</p>
<p> Turkey		  2,010	    1,475</p>
<p> China		   1,500	    1,403</p>
<p> USA		     3,630	    3,553</p>
<p> TOTAL BEET	   37,609	   36,358</p>
<p>CANE sugar output</p>
<p>	     estimate 1996/97	  1995/96</p>
<p> Cuba		    4,250	    4,525</p>
<p> Brazil		 14,775	   13,594</p>
<p> Mexico		  4,650	    4,729</p>
<p> Indonesia	     2,400	    2,276</p>
<p> India		  14,240	   17,883</p>
<p> Thailand		6,075	    6,323</p>
<p> China		   5,700	    5,367</p>
<p> Pakistan		2,550	    2,663</p>
<p> Philippines	   1,875	    1,853</p>
<p> Australia	     5,620	    5,133</p>
<p> TOTAL CANE	   85,195	   86,984</p>
<p> WORLD TOTAL	 122,804	  123,342</p>
<p>Key sugar CONSUMPTION figures</p>
<p>	     estimate 1997	     1996</p>
<p> EU TOTAL	     14,500	   14,525</p>
<p> Russia		  5,800	    5,550</p>
<p> ex-USSR TOTAL	10,307	   10,277</p>
<p> Turkey		  1,955	    1,915</p>
<p> EUROPE TOTAL	 31,535	   31,372</p>
<p> Mexico		  4,100	    4,250</p>
<p> USA		     8,855	    8,735</p>
<p> Brazil		  8,500	    8,300</p>
<p> N/C. AMERICA TOTAL 16,851	   16,779</p>
<p> S.AMERICA TOTAL    14,372	   13,965</p>
<p> China		   8,600	    8,500</p>
<p> India		  15,200	   14,750</p>
<p> Indonesia	     3,364	    3,252</p>
<p> Pakistan		3,000	    2,935</p>
<p> ASIA TOTAL	   46,068	   44,893</p>
<p> AFRICA TOTAL	 10,401	   10,079</p>
<p> WORLD TOTAL	 120,444	  118,282</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
